cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PolSejAn in your research, please cite this software."
title: "PolSejAn: A MATLAB Application for Polarimetric Time–Frequency Analysis of Seismic Signals"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-21

authors:
  - family-names: "Abratkiewicz"
    given-names: "Karol"
    affiliation: "Warsaw University of Technology"

  - family-names: "Mendecki"
    given-names: "Maciej"
    affiliation: "University of Silesia in Katowice"

abstract: >
  PolSejAn is a MATLAB App Designer application for time–frequency
  and polarimetric analysis of three-component seismic signals.
  It supports EW, NS, and VZ signal components, Gaussian-window
  STFT analysis, Stokes parameter calculation, band-pass filtering,
  decimation, back-azimuth compensation, and automatic window
  optimization using Renyi entropy.

keywords:
  - seismic signal processing
  - time-frequency analysis
  - polarization analysis
  - Stokes parameters
  - short-time Fourier transform
  - MATLAB
